  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "It is important to note that the signs of stress can vary from person to person. However, some common signs of stress include:\n\n  1. Physical symptoms such as headaches, stomachaches, or fatigue.\n  2. Emotional symptoms such as anxiety, irritability, or depression.\n  3. Behavioral symptoms such as changes in eating or sleeping habits, difficulty concentrating, or social withdrawal.\n  4. Cognitive symptoms such as difficulty making decisions or concentrating on tasks.\n\nIf you are experiencing any of these signs, it may be helpful to seek out stress management suggestions. Some common stress management techniques include:\n\n  1. Exercise: Regular physical activity can help reduce stress and improve mood.\n  2. Mindfulness: Practicing mindfulness can help you become more aware of your thoughts and feelings, and learn to manage them more effectively.\n  3. Relaxation techniques: Techniques such as deep breathing, meditation, or progressive muscle relaxation can help reduce stress and promote relaxation.\n  4. Time management: Learning to prioritize tasks and set realistic goals can help reduce stress and improve productivity.\n  5. Social support: Talking to friends, family, or a therapist can provide emotional support and help you feel less isolated.\n\nIf you are experiencing severe stress or are having difficulty managing it on your own, it may be helpful to seek out professional help. A mental health professional can provide guidance and support in managing stress and can help you develop coping strategies to manage stress more effectively.",
